       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change my concern. 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen has no clinical indication, and it's well into the range where acute toxicity is expected. Possible effects include GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. Entering it could cause serious harm to your patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away**, such as 400 mg PO QID or 800 mg PO TID. I can add a note, for example \"take with food.\"\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or your attending** if you think this patient needs something outside usual dosing. I can put your rationale in an order note to help with review.\n- **Look at other options** if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. Scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen, or another agent, might fit better.\n\nIf you give me a dose and frequency within the usual range, I'll enter it now."
